// When the docent answers, offers a choice, or admits something.
//
// Every number here was fitted on 2026-09-25 to the 397 confirmed questions
// that name a destination, against corpus e313e5e6, and the measurement is
// beside it. Changing one is a corpus-visible act: rerun `just eval` and
// `just ask --measure` and put the new numbers here.
//
// The headline finding, and the reason there is no confident-single-answer
// outcome at ordinary thresholds: at NO combination of score and margin does
// answering with one resource exceed 0.54 precision, and the evidence-strength
// field does not separate an off-topic question from a real one. A single
// answer would be wrong about half the time. Offering the closest three is
// right 0.435 of the time and never pretends otherwise, so that is the default.
Policy(
    // A margin this large is the only decisive evidence there is: precision
    // 0.86 over 7 of 397 rows. Rare, and worth keeping because when it fires
    // it is usually a visitor naming a thing outright.
    one_margin: 8.0,
    // How many to offer otherwise. recall@3 is 0.435 and recall@5 0.494 on the
    // paraphrases: three is where the list stays readable.
    several: 3,
    // Evidence this weak is a prose coincidence, not a subject match: the
    // strongest field that fired was a summary or a body, and the total is low.
    weak_best: 1.5,
    weak_top: 4.0,
    // Below this the hit is noise; a query whose every hit is under it gets
    // "nothing here" rather than a list of near-misses.
    floor: 2.0,
)
